// The solver must be deterministic given the same inputs and seed, so that a
// layout a user saved or printed can be reproduced exactly. Math.random() would
// break that silently - the layout would still be valid, just different every
// run, which no test would catch. Use the seeded PRNG in src/solver/rng.ts.
//
// Biome has no native no-restricted-properties equivalent, so this is a GritQL
// plugin. Plugins apply repo-wide rather than per-directory, which is fine here:
// nothing else in this codebase has a legitimate reason to call Math.random()
// either.
`$fn($args)` where {
  $fn <: `Math.random`,
  register_diagnostic(span=$fn, message="Use the seeded PRNG in src/solver/rng.ts - the solver must be deterministic.", severity="error")
}
